            <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-item__a" x-show="open === 1" x-cloak x-transition>
            <p>Your staff don't need to change their workflow much – they log bookings, record payments, and request discounts. The difference is those actions are now tracked, approved, and visible. The interface is built for the front desk, not for software engineers.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item reveal" data-delay="3" :class="{ 'faq-item--open': open === 2 }">
          <button class="faq-item__q" @click="open = open === 2 ? null : 2" :aria-expanded="open === 2">
            We're not big enough for a system like this.
            <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-item__a" x-show="open === 2" x-cloak x-transition>
            <p>If you have more than one branch and more than five staff members, you're already big enough to feel the pain this solves. The right time to build systems is before things break – not after.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item reveal" data-delay="4" :class="{ 'faq-item--open': open === 3 }">
          <button class="faq-item__q" @click="open = open === 3 ? null : 3" :aria-expanded="open === 3">
            Can we see it before committing?
            <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-item__a" x-show="open === 3" x-cloak x-transition>
            <p>Yes. We'll show you a live walkthrough tailored to your branch setup in 20 minutes. No slides. No sales pressure. Just the product.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

